    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000147357179": {
      "title": "Student: Film & Media Technical Assistant, 2026-27",
      "description": "In this hands-on role, you will: Assist in the management, maintenance, and use of film and new media equipment This position serves the film program, the new media program, and the graphic design program. You will respond to the needs of faculty and students in all programs and follow a consistent protocol for equipment use Checking out and checking in of film, new media, and design equipment Ensuring proper use and care of the equipment during class and out of class (as requested) Monitoring the editing suites Providing technical assistance to those using the equipment when possible Working on special projects. \n\n Enrolled as a student at Augsburg University and be work-study eligible Have a working knowledge of film cameras, video cameras, DSLR cameras, audio equipment, lighting gear, computers, and the Premiere Pro software package Highly responsible, detail driven, and self-motivated Excellent troubleshooting skills Ability to follow established protocol Ability to lift up to 50 pounds Ability to work independently Some evenings and weekend hours are expected \n\n All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume Cover Letter (optional) Augsburg University is an Equal Opportunity employer.  We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, creed, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability, military service, protected veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. \nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact the Human Resources department by phone at  612.330.1058 or email at hr@augsburg.edu.  Human Resources is located at 20 Memorial Hall. \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our student explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.",
      "department": "Communication Studies, Film and New Media"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000147353589": {
      "title": "Student: SoNS Lab Safety Technician 2026-27",
      "description": "STEM at Augsburg University has a large physical footprint with teaching and research labs split between the basement and four floors of the Hagfors Center. The Student Lab Safety Technician (SLST) will help ensure all labs meet the OSHA standards have the necessary safety tests, first aid supplies as well as meeting the monthly visual safety checks to maintain safe lab work environments. The SLST will be trained and required to weekly visit and document the lab safety equipment in all STEM. The SLST will report to and work directly with the Biology Lab Manager, Chris Palahniuk and the Chemistry Stock Room Tech, Isaiah Ripley. School of Natural Sciences Laboratory Work Includes: Monthly safety checks and documentation of School of Natural Sciences laboratory safety equipment including eyewash stations, safety showers Monthly School of Natural Sciences laboratory checks for safety compliance, unsafe lab conditions and visual inspection of hazardous waste storage Monthly First Aid Box checks and documentation of contents Other duties may be assigned as we grow into this position, and in updated communication with the student hire' Compensation & Benefits: $16.45/hr Minnesota Sick and Safe Time Minnesota Paid Family and Medical Leave Not eligible for health insurance benefits \n  \n\n Currently enrolled as a student at Augsburg University and be work-study eligible School of Natural Sciences majors with STEM lab experience (like any or all of CHM115, BIO151 or PHY107/PHY121) are preferred. At least one year of School of Natural Sciences course work preferred Excellent oral communication and oservational skills Good written communication skills Ability to work independently and reliable Some understanding of lab safety standards helpful Other safety experience preferred Comprehensive laboratory safety training and lab orientation will be supplied including OSHA standards for Lab Safety. Basic duties will include lifting light loads, activating water showers and supporting a large shower tester above your head, pushing a cart and privileged access to sensitive lab areas.   Schedule 5 hours per week, flexible, but preference towards weekly shift work - from August to May \n\n All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume Cover Letter (optional) Augsburg University is an Equal Opportunity employer.  We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, creed, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability, military service, protected veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. \nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact the Human Resources department by phone at  612.330.1058 or email at hr@augsburg.edu.  Human Resources is located at 20 Memorial Hall. \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our student explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.",
      "department": "School of Natural Sciences"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/AugsburgUniversity-MinneapolisMN/744000147081524": {
      "title": "Student: Institutional Advancement Office Assistant, 2026-27",
      "description": "Administrative duties include: Checking emails, answering phone calls, data entry, general office work, etc. Covering the front desk while our administrative assistant is away from the desk. Data entry  Updating our database, including but not limited to, address updates, researching and adding birth dates and death dates, adding education information. Maintaining our database like making entries uniform, researching and adding information.  Assist with office tasks like soring the mail, organizing the office and putting files and office supplies where they go. Assist with filing both electronic and paper files Assist with scanning documents to the cloud for long term storage. Assist with making receipt letters for our donors, then stuffing them into envelopes and mailing them. Special Projects As Assigned Approximately 60% of the work will be done on a desk on a computer or stuffing envelopes. \nApproximately 20% of the work will be moving around, carrying or organizing items under 20 lbs. \nApproximately 20% will be standing.  Compensation and Benefits Rate of Pay: $16.45/hour Minnesota Sick and Safe Time Minnesota Paid Family and Medical Leave Not eligible for health insurance benefits   \n\n An ideal candidate will be Be passionate about philanthropy Be very detail oriented and highly organized Be able to follow through on tasks.  Strong communicator, both written and verbal, able to relate well to a wide variety of people in multiple settings Detail oriented and highly organized Maintain confidentiality with sensitive information High customer service orientation Skilled in the use of Google platform, Microsoft Excel, Word, PowerPoint Must be comfortable working in Google Drive, Sheets and Docs Be able to ask for help when needed  Requirements: Must be enrolled at Augsburg University Must have work-study as part of financial aid award. Please see your financial aid award letter, or contact student financial services if you have questions: studentfinances@augsburg.edu \n\n All student applicants must attach the following for consideration:  Resume Cover Letter (optional) Augsburg University is an Equal Opportunity employer.  We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity to all applicants and employees regardless of their race, creed, color, religion, gender, age, national origin, disability, military service, protected veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, transgender status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. \nIf you need a reasonable accommodation to complete our application process, please contact the Human Resources department by phone at  612.330.1058 or email at hr@augsburg.edu.  Human Resources is located at 20 Memorial Hall. \n\n Augsburg University is committed to helping our student explore their vocation. As a University with a calling, we welcome the unique gifts that each of our employees brings to our collective work, and we are committed to supporting our students as they seek to match those gifts with the needs of the University and our larger community.    Student employment with Augsburg is more than a job - it is an opportunity for Augsburg students to gain meaningful work experience in a supportive setting that promotes professional growth, personal accountability, teamwork and collaboration and quality work that lives up to our mission of educating students to be informed citizens, thoughtful stewards, critical thinkers, and responsible leaders.",
      "department": "Advancement Services"
